post.description:
Creates a job to retrieve data from the payroll system. The body of this request specifies the resource, and optionally a nested sub-resource, of which data are to be fetched. 

The following resources can be fetched: absences, client-data, employees, employment-periods, gross-payments, month-records und hourly-wages.
All resources include their subresources, i.e. client-data contains salary-types, employees their personal-data etc.

If the "id" is omitted for employees or month-records in the top-level resource, all employees' data will be fetched.
Absences can only be fetched as a sub-resource of one employee (one request per employee necessary).
I.e. the body
{
	"resource_name": "client-data",
	"reference_date": "2023-01"
}
fetches all client data (which client is specificed in the URL).
{
	"resource_name": "employees",
	"reference_date": "2023-01"
}
fetches all employees for a client (which client is specificed in the URL).
{
	"resource_name": "employees",
	"id": "1",
	"reference_date": "2023-01"
}
fetches the employee with the personnel number 1 while
{
	"resource_name": "employees",
	"id": "1",
	"sub_resource": {
		"resource_name": "gross-payments",
		"id": "2",
		"reference_date": "2023-01"
	}
}
fetches the gross-payment with the id 2 belonging to the employee with the personnel number 1.
Month-Records examples: {
	"resource_name": "month-records",
	"reference_date": "2023-01"
}
fetches all month records for a client and the given month while
{
	"resource_name": "employees",
	"id": "1",
	"sub_resource": {
		"resource_name": "month-records",
		"reference_date": "2023-01"
	}
}
fetches all month records for the employee with the personnel number 1 for the given month.

The reference-date has to be given in the body, only in the lowest sub-resource in the hierarchy.

The resource can be fetched asynchronously from the result endpoint for the corresponding job after having been received from the payroll system.
If there are RestHooks registered under the same client-id, these will be triggered when the job was completed.
